ary tuberculosis cases</p></caption><graphic xlink:href="jkms-24-592-i001"/><table-wrap-foot><fn><p>INH, isoniazid; RFP, rifampicin; EMB, ethambutol; PZA, pyrazinamide.</p></fn></table-wrap-foot></table-wrap><table-wrap id="T2" position="float"><label>Table 2</label><caption><p>Clinical characteristics of young Korean soldiers with pulmonary tuberculosis with or without multi-drug resistance (MDR)</p></caption><graphic xlink:href="jkms-24-592-i002"/><table-wrap-foot><fn><p>AFB, acid-fast bacilli; CT, computed tomography; OR, odds ratio; CI, confidence interval.</p></fn></table-wrap-foot></table-wrap></floats-group></article>